## ─── COI-6 — self_cancel() atomicity (after COI-5 lands) ───────────────────
# File: trade_monitor.py (lines 362-367)
#
> Read trade_monitor.py self_cancel(). It currently sets STATE_ARCHIVED before
> writing the archive file — two failure modes:
>   (1) archive succeeds, unlink() fails → monitor re-enters loop
>   (2) archive fails → state already ARCHIVED → infinite retry
>
> Rewrite self_cancel() to:
>   1. Call atomic_write_json(self._archive_path, self._to_dict()) first.
>      If it returns False: log error, leave monitor intact, return False.
>      Do NOT set state.
>   2. Try self._path.unlink(). If OSError: log warning, continue.
>   3. Set self.state = STATE_ARCHIVED ONLY after archive confirmed.
>   4. Return True.
>
> Add two tests to tests/test_slo_save.py:
>   - test_self_cancel_no_state_on_archive_failure: mock atomic_write_json
>     -> False, assert state != STATE_ARCHIVED
>   - test_self_cancel_state_set_even_if_unlink_fails: mock unlink ->
>     PermissionError, assert state == STATE_ARCHIVED, result is True
>
> Run pytest tests/ -x -q and show output.

